'''The Covenant combines formidable technical infrastructure with differentiated biological roles and useful labor. The best-guess zero variant preserves that distinction: engineered Huragok doing maintenance, excavation or medicine are working persons, not automatic output that can be ignored. Technical potential does not establish a common release from labor or a universal necessities floor. Guarantees are estimated as weak across the unequal member population, with broad uncertainty about local rights.

Organic religious and political elites concentrate productive power. A capable artificial biological species is not the same as an independent AI government. The modest nonworking estimate includes dependents and some elite leisure while retaining real maintenance, care, industry, administration and military activity. It does not convert fleet strength or species proportions into a census. The broad original-Covenant scope is an inferred model checked against a narrower role reference, and post-collapse splinter institutions are not silently treated as identical.''',
